From f73d87ef3d5bde846c2dda71ea0a765f4c6bd822 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: letress <212964567+letress@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:43:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 25/95] clk: samsung: exynos9610: Parent CMGP USI/I2C gates to
 their dividers

Each CMGP USI and the shared CMGP I2C clock has a mux followed by a
divider (CLK_CON_DIV_DIV_CLK_CMGP_USI0x, CLK_CON_DIV_DIV_CLK_CMGP_I2C).
The gates behind them are parented to the mux, so the divider is left
out of the tree: the rate reported for the IP clock ignores the divider
and a rate request from a serial or I2C driver cannot reach it.

In the vendor kernel's clock tables
(drivers/soc/samsung/cal-if/exynos9610/cmucal-node.c and cmucal-sfr.c)
the parent of the USI_CMGP0x IPCLK and CLK_CMGP_USI0x gates is
DIV_CLK_CMGP_USI0x and the parent of the I2C_CMGP0x IPCLK gates is
DIV_CLK_CMGP_I2C.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
